\ Arithmetic checks for exact decimal division and binomial counts.
\ Small intermediate divisions never discard fractions: each step
\ of the multiplicative binomial identity is already an integer.

The dividedtest is a wide quantity.

To check the long small division:
  Put "121515484051014339000" into the dividedtest.
  Divide the dividedtest by 17 and retain the remainder.
  If the dividedtest is not "7147969650059667000",
    put "Long division by seventeen has the wrong quotient." into the check report; exit.
  If the small division remainder is not 0,
    put "Long division of an exact multiple returned a remainder." into the check report; exit.
  Put "170141183460469231731687303715884105727" into the dividedtest.
  Divide the dividedtest by 10 and retain the remainder.
  If the dividedtest is not "17014118346046923173168730371588410572",
    put "Long division by ten has the wrong quotient." into the check report; exit.
  If the small division remainder is not 7,
    put "Long division by ten returned the wrong remainder." into the check report; exit.

To check the binomial coefficients:
  Calculate binomial coefficients given 5 and 0.
  If the binomial result is not "1",
    put "C(5,0) is not one." into the check report; exit.
  Calculate binomial coefficients given 5 and 2.
  If the binomial result is not "10",
    put "C(5,2) is not ten." into the check report; exit.
  Calculate binomial coefficients given 15 and 6.
  If the binomial result is not "5005",
    put "C(15,6) is wrong." into the check report; exit.
  Calculate binomial coefficients given 50 and 15.
  If the binomial result is not "2250829575120",
    put "C(50,15) is wrong." into the check report; exit.
  Calculate binomial coefficients given 130 and 16.
  If the binomial result is not "121515484051014339000",
    put "C(130,16) lost big-number precision." into the check report; exit.
  Calculate binomial coefficients given 10 and 11.
  If the binomial result is not "0",
    put "An impossible binomial coefficient was not zero." into the check report; exit.
